<urn:beads-cache:finding:ARCH-001> triage:id "ARCH-001" ; triage:sprint "c-1" ; triage:severity "BLOCKING" ; triage:location "crates/bd-cache-sync/Cargo.toml:31" ; triage:source "qa-3 owning reviewer fenced JSON" ; triage:status "open" ; triage:record "{\"adr\": \"ADR-BDC-0016\", \"description\": \"OPEN/BLOCKED at QA3. The direct bd-cache-sync -> sc-command receiver dependency remains at Cargo.toml:31 and cron_log.rs:3; it is outside ADR-BDC-0016:1148 and the approved phase plan:122, which permit only the dependency carried by published sc-cron. No approved amendment or waiver was introduced. The strict introducer-aware graph gate is byte-for-byte unchanged from QA2 and still rejects this candidate production edge. The QA3 changes are health test code and sprint/admin receipts; they do not resolve the public logging-seam gap already verified in QA2. ARCH-001 remains correlated with RBQA-F001 and the actual-graph finding QA2-001; those IDs remain independent and are not reissued by this scope-locked architecture review.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-sync/Cargo.toml\", \"id\": \"ARCH-001\", \"line\": 31, \"remediation\": \"Keep ARCH-001 open and do not merge this candidate under the current ADR. An authorized upstream public receiver/type adapter or equivalent public callback constructor must permit the logging bridge without the direct sync -> sc-command edge; then remove that edge and verify the existing strict graph gate. Any baseline or architectural exception change requires separate explicit authorization and an Approved/Active ADR amendment. Retain the strengthened gate and required scheduler logging; no workaround or waiver is authorized by this QA disposition.\", \"reviewer\": \"arch-qa\", \"rule\": \"RULE-ADR-CODE\", \"severity\": \"BLOCKING\"}" .
